WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.588 --> 00:00:03.421
(audience applauds)

00:00:03.421 --> 00:00:04.690
- Oh, hi.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:09.020
It's time for one of mt
favorite segments, "Dear Drew."

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.600
All right, I put out a
call to action for people

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.503
to send an actual snail mail.

00:00:14.503 --> 00:00:17.720
And much to our surprise and delight,

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.480
we got a ton of mail.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.900
And I want to get to our letters,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.890
but first I'd love to celebrate
our zip code of the day,

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.630
33916 in Fort Myers, Florida.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.440
(audience applauds)

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.273
That's right.

00:00:32.273 --> 00:00:37.273
It's also home to our local
CBS affiliate, WINK TV.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.400
I don't know if you saw the show earlier,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.476
but animals love it.

00:00:41.476 --> 00:00:42.710
(audience laughs)

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:46.401
Fort Myers is home to the only
seashell museum in the world.

00:00:46.401 --> 00:00:50.215
And I know, by the way,
I needed to see that,

00:00:50.215 --> 00:00:53.330
and it was also the winter vacation spot

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.910
of Thomas Edison.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.930
That's right, the dude who
invented the light bulb.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.000
Who knew he was a snowbird?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.280
Which I just learned means
you don't like the cold

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.660
so you go warm for winter.
(audience laughs)

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.310
Send us some letters, please,

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.270
we'd love to open them on the show,

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.980
as we are going to do right now.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.263
Letter number one, hello.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.706
This is from Autumn in
Waltonville, Illinois.

00:01:17.706 --> 00:01:19.457
Oh, hold on.

00:01:19.457 --> 00:01:20.607
"Dear Drew, I wanted to write you,

00:01:20.607 --> 00:01:23.893
"and introduce my incredibly
amazing mom, Wendy,

00:01:27.847 --> 00:01:28.680
"mom of four,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.610
"and longtime essential worker
of the US Postal Service."

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.463
Oh my gosh, this is so apropos!

00:01:35.547 --> 00:01:37.557
"I have always loved my mom so much.

00:01:37.557 --> 00:01:39.787
"And I thought that you
and I were sister spirits,

00:01:39.787 --> 00:01:42.547
"and she's celebrating her
46th birthday this week.

00:01:42.547 --> 00:01:45.160
"Would you maybe give
her some kind words?"

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.500
Well, Wendy, I love what you do.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.120
And I thank you for delivering the mail

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.940
because you deliver love
every day and necessities.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.640
So thank you for everything you do.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.670
Go USPS.
(audience applauds)

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.520
I love you.
(audience applauds)

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.350
I am that guy who totally,
like, stops at every person

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:09.377
I'm like, "Yeah!" and
they're like, "Okay, cool."

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.070
Okay, this is letter number two.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.210
This is from Nico in
Los Angeles, California.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.260
Oh, my old hometown.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.093
All right.

00:02:18.093 --> 00:02:20.667
She writes, "Growing up everyone called me

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:21.950
"a Drew look-alike."

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:26.100
Uh, Nico, you freaking me out.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.300
Like, is this a Photoshop thing?

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.050
I mean, this is crazy.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.620
Look at this.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.160
We are the same person. (screams)

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:35.993
Okay.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.683
Thank you so much.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:40.663
That was Nico.

00:02:40.663 --> 00:02:41.496
Thank you.

00:02:41.496 --> 00:02:42.370
Okay.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.560
Look, I'm sorting through the mail,

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:44.860
it's not a perfect system.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:51.060
Okay, this is from Raquel
and she's from Salem, Oregon.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.030
Oh, I love Oregon.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:53.863
All right, "Dear Drew.

00:02:53.863 --> 00:02:56.680
"I love that you're bringing
the written word back."

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.000
Thank you.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.393
To you and your animals.

00:03:00.277 --> 00:03:02.357
"Thank you for sharing the positivity.

00:03:02.357 --> 00:03:07.097
"And I happen to have a
medical bill for blood work,

00:03:07.097 --> 00:03:08.875
"and it's been really hard times

00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:11.097
"and I've struggled to pay this.

00:03:11.097 --> 00:03:13.447
"Thank you for taking the time to read it,

00:03:13.447 --> 00:03:15.876
"and thank you for all that you're doing."

00:03:15.876 --> 00:03:17.520
All right, Raquel,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.470
I don't want you to
stress over this anymore.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.880
I want you to take care of yourself.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.209
So I'm going to pay your medical bill.

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:26.380
(audience applauds)

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.110
If anyone out there has
a bill, needs advice,

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.560
'cause I live to give advice,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.210
look, we're all better advisors
to others than ourselves,

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.610
and I'm all about self improvement.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:39.880
So, god, "Dear Drew," I
loved "Dear Abby" so much,

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.520
so, you know, any kind of stuff like that,

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.420
that hearkens back to a tradition
I've always been a fan of.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.060
If you wanna tell me a joke,

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.510
send me a fun family photo, I'm game.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.780
Mail me any thoughts, questions, requests,

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.570
heartfelt funny story.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.390
All right, I can't wait to
read more of your letters

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:03.120
on this show and thank you
to my "Dear Drew" pen pals,

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.360
Autumn, Nico, and Raquel.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.420
All right, I am going to be
putting these, oh God, stamps.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.850
You have no idea how much I love stamps.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.670
All right, I'm putting stamps on.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:17.810
I'm gonna mail these in
the mailbox right now.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.520
This is how much I love mail.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:20.650
I have a mailbox.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:21.483
All right?

00:04:21.483 --> 00:04:24.130
That should kind of show you
where I'm at with this thing.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.253
Here we go.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.480
It's been sent.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:31.436
We'll be right back.
(audience applauds)

00:04:31.436 --> 00:04:34.103
(upbeat music)

